# Trivy ignore file — vulnerability suppressions WITH RATIONALE (audit P2-M1).
#
# Rules:
#   - Every entry MUST document why the finding is safe to ignore.
#   - Prefer fixing over ignoring. Only suppress non-actionable / unreachable
#     findings (no fix available to us, or not exploitable in our usage).
#   - Re-review every entry when the relevant base image is bumped.

# CVE-2026-43494 — linux-libc-dev, in the upstream roundcube/roundcubemail
# (Debian) base used by the webmail image. This package provides only Linux
# kernel *header files* for compiling against; there is no running kernel
# inside the container, so the vulnerability is not reachable at runtime.
# We cannot patch it directly — it ships from the upstream base image and
# clears when Roundcube republishes. Re-check on the next roundcube base bump.
CVE-2026-43494
